course: dictionary
lesson: 15537
title: Words that show a mood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show how someone feels without saying it outright. Sullenly is one of them. It is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. «She answered sullenly» tells you how she answered: not kindly, but in a grumpy, silent way.
explain: Look at the words around sullenly for clues. «He shrugged, folded his arms and stared at the floor.» Folded arms, staring and not speaking are all signs of sulking, so sullenly means in a bad-tempered, silent and unfriendly way.
explain: Sullenly can also describe weather or water. «Dark clouds moved sullenly across the sky.» Clouds cannot sulk, but the word makes the sky feel gloomy and heavy. Check by swapping in your meaning: does gloomy fit the sentence? It does, so you have understood it.
fact: Sullenly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Sullenly» means in a bad-tempered, silent and unfriendly way, as when someone is sulking.
fact: «Sullenly» can also describe dark, gloomy weather or water, such as «the river flowed sullenly».
fact: Good clues for sullen moods are folded arms, a silent face and short, grumpy answers.
exercise: «He answered sullenly and kept his eyes on the floor.» How did he answer? | *Grumpily and without saying much | Kindly, to help his friend | Quickly, with a big smile | Happily and loudly
exercise: «Dark clouds moved sullenly over the hills.» What does sullenly suggest about the clouds? | Light and fluffy | Bright and cheerful | *Gloomy and heavy | Fast and windy
exercise: «She sat sullenly in the corner, arms folded.» Which clue shows she is not happy? | The corner | She sat | Sat down | *Arms folded
test: «The boy replied sullenly when his mum asked him to tidy up.» What is the boy's mood? | Excited | Silly | Sleepy | *Cross and unwilling to talk
test: «Grey water lapped sullenly against the old boat.» What does sullenly show about the water? | *Dark and gloomy | Warm and fast | Bubbly and fun | Sparkling and bright
exam: «Her friends laughed, but Mia just stared sullenly at the table.» Why do we know Mia is sulking? | She is running to the shops | She is singing happily | She laughed at the joke | *She stares, says nothing and looks unfriendly
